From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:49:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/61] NNS.stack: score the "ALL" Method 1 candidate with the
 deployed estimator

In the Method 1 n.best search the ALL candidate was scored out-of-fold as
a constant prediction, mean(training y), but when ALL won the final fit
was NNS.reg(n.best = "all") (multivariate) or the univariate NNS.reg
fit, both non-constant estimators. Model selection therefore compared
the local candidates against a model that was never deployed, and
OBJfn.reg reported the SSE of a constant mean.

Score ALL in every fold with the estimator used for the final fit:
NNS.reg(..., n.best = "all", point.only = TRUE) for multivariate designs
and the univariate NNS.reg fit (.fit_univariate_raw) for one column.

Before -> after (pure-noise y, n = 160 training rows, seed 5, method = 1):
  univariate:   ALL wins, OBJfn.reg 192.79 (constant-mean SSE), n.best NA
                -> local k = 6 wins, OBJfn.reg 204.65 (ALL's real OOF is worse)
  multivariate: ALL wins, OBJfn.reg 192.79 -> ALL wins, OBJfn.reg 190.37
                (OOF of NNS.reg(n.best = "all")), n.best 156
Final predictions are unchanged in these cases; iris and Boston Method 1
fits (where a local k wins) are unchanged. The selected n.best and
OBJfn.reg change wherever ALL was involved in the decision.
---
 R/Stack.R | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/R/Stack.R b/R/Stack.R
index 26159ae..d582922 100644
--- a/R/Stack.R
+++ b/R/Stack.R
@@ -1277,11 +1277,10 @@ NNS.stack <- function(IVs.train,
         }
         
         # ALL is the separate full-support limit condition and is always
-        # evaluated, irrespective of the later local stopping point.
-        all_raw <- rep(
-          mean(train_y_fit) - response_offset,
-          length(test_x)
-        )
+        # evaluated, irrespective of the later local stopping point. Score the
+        # estimator that is deployed when ALL wins (the univariate NNS.reg
+        # fit), not a constant training mean.
+        all_raw <- .fit_univariate_raw(train_x, train_y_fit, test_x)$raw
         good <- is.finite(all_raw)
         if (any(good)) {
           rows <- valid_idx[good]
@@ -1356,12 +1355,28 @@ NNS.stack <- function(IVs.train,
           }
         }
         
-        # Preserve the current full-support limit behavior from this version:
-        # all RPM points reduce to the balanced fitting-response mean. The ALL
-        # candidate is always populated for every fold.
-        all_raw <- rep(
-          mean(train_y_fit) - response_offset,
-          length(valid_idx)
+        # The ALL candidate is always populated for every fold. Score the
+        # estimator that is deployed when ALL wins, NNS.reg(n.best = "all"),
+        # rather than a constant training mean.
+        all_fit <- suppressWarnings(
+          NNS.reg(
+            train_design,
+            train_y_fit,
+            point.est = valid_design,
+            plot = FALSE,
+            residual.plot = FALSE,
+            n.best = "all",
+            order = order,
+            type = NULL,
+            factor.2.dummy = FALSE,
+            dist = dist,
+            ncores = ncores,
+            point.only = TRUE
+          )
+        )
+        all_raw <- .sanitize_raw(
+          as.numeric(all_fit$Point.est) - response_offset,
+          y[train_idx]
         )
         good <- is.finite(all_raw)
         if (any(good)) {
